	{
		"DESCRIPTION": "Flat-top HEX ground tileset, extracted 2026-09-06 from region temp2's GROUND ONLY: 74 unique hexes from a 20x10 lattice. Buildings are deliberately absent -- the cut was taken from WorldMapProps' patched ground, which paints the nine structures out (7 houses, 2 towers), and the extraction verified 482 building-only pixels in the source art against 0 in this sheet. Houses and towers return later as placed objects, not as ground pixels. GEOMETRY: a flat-top hex pre-stretched for pitch 60 has a SQUARE world footprint, so each frame is 16x16 with hex vertices on whole pixels at (16,8) (12,16) (4,16) (0,8) (4,0) (12,0) and every slanted edge a 1:2 pixel slope. The MAP lattice is hex -- columns every 12 px, rows every 16 px, odd columns dropped 8 px -- but the SHEET is still a rectangular grid of 16 px frames, which is why the existing importer, content hashes and id ledger read it unchanged. Extracted from square-drawn art as a prototype starting point: the content inside each hex was authored for square cells, so hex-native art will supersede it.",
